---
import RecipeLayout from '../../layouts/RecipeLayout.astro';
---
<RecipeLayout title="Laminated Pastry Base">
  <div class="recipe-title-block">
    <h1>Laminated Pastry Base</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Still proofing — check back soon.</p>
  </div>

  <main>
    <section class="block">
      <div class="callout">
        <p>This one's still in the oven, so to speak. The Laminated Pastry Base is the croissant-family foundation behind Bruce's Breads' Pastry &amp; Lamination section — a stiff, white-flour-leaning levain (45–50% hydration, 20% of flour weight) softened directly into cold milk before the flour goes in, then given 8–12 hours to peak before the détrempe is built, folded, and turned.</p>
        <p>The test bake is done and it's close — Bruce has one small adjustment left to make before this base is ready to call finished. Once that's settled, the full write-up follows: recipe card, step-by-step tutorial, ingredient history, and a baking playlist, the same treatment every other recipe on this site gets.</p>
        <p>In the meantime, the site's <a href="/guides/">baking Guides</a> have plenty on the technique behind it — the <a href="/guides/starter/starter-vs-levain/">Starter vs. Levain</a> guide covers why this base uses a stiff starter in the first place, and the <a href="/guides/starter/starter-types-and-flours/">Starter Types and Flours</a> guide has the hydration math behind it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</RecipeLayout>
